  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 132 AM CDT Thu Oct 22 2026\n\nWeather pattern shifts this weekend into next week as the upper low \ncontinues to slowly approach the region before opening up into a \nwave that moves across the central Plains early next week. Models \nalso show a cold front moving across the area early next week. This \nsystem will bring a chance for showers and maybe some storms Sunday \ninto Tuesday with the highest chances over western parts of the fa. \nIt still looks like moisture with this system will not be as \nabundant as the last couple of rain events that the area has had \nwhich means lower rainfall amounts expected overall compared to \nthose events. Ensembles are showing 90th percentile (reasonable \nworst case scenario) rainfall amounts of 1-2 inches possible in \nwestern parts of the fa. However, right now it looks like most \nlocations in the fa are expected to see less than an inch of rain.\n\nTemperatures are expected to remain above normal until Tuesday when \ntemperatures drop closer to normal as cooler air moves into the \nregion behind the cold front.",
